ire additional teachers or bus  or bus drivers at this point we're  talking about make sure that we're  talking about  that well they have to plan over the  period of time i'm sure i don't want my  kids to be going to school where they  have to fire teachers next year  or won't have to be able to do the  facilities facility upgrades i should  say  necessary in order to ensure they're  going to school safely  that's exactly what is included in this  package  uh let me turn to another subject about  the bill now that the senate  parliamentarian has ruled that the  15 dollar minimum wage does not qualify  under the budget rules some senate  democrats are talking about either using  tax incentives or tax penalties  to get corporations and small businesses  to go there as part of the coveted  relief bill  does the president support that  well i think you're referring to senator  sanders proposal chris and we have not  yet reviewed that proposal but the  senate  the president supports exactly what  senator sanders does which is  increasing the minimum wage for the  american people for workers who are just  trying to make ends meet  and he thinks that's long overdue we're  going to have to spend the next several  days or even weeks figuring out what the  best path forward is but he's committed  to doing that  you also had a busy week in foreign  policy and i want to talk about that  during the campaign  candidate biden said that he promised to  crack down on saudi arabia  for the murder of jamal khashoggi here  he is  we were going to in fact make them pay  the price and  make them in fact the pariah that they  are there's very little social redeeming  value  of the in the present government in  saudi arabia  and on friday u.s intelligence agencies  released this report  we assess that saudi arabia's crown  prince mohammed bin salman  approved an operation in istanbul turkey  to capture or kill saudi journalist  jamal khashoggi  couple of questions jen does the  president 