 the region this  is not the time to come  and this is a difficult choice for  everyone but as a mother as a parent  i'm not going to support not nor would  the president sending kids under 18 some  at the age of 11 12  13 back on a treacherous trip across the  border to face persecution  and difficult circumstances in their  country these kids are coming alone  and this is a this is the choice we've  made because we feel it's humane and we  feel  safe the vast majority of any family  that's coming together  any adults that's coming are turned away  at the border  because we have not had time to put in  place comprehensive immigration policies  yet at this point in time finally  when will the white house pull the  nomination of nira tanda  to be the budget director  well chris we remain committed to  fighting our hearts out for near  tandon we believe she is the right  person she's qualified she's experienced  to lead  the budget department she brings unique  experience as somebody who's lived  through  uh benefiting from a number of these  programs and she's worked on these  issues for decades  across the aisle so we're going to keep  fighting for it we knew that some of  these fights would be difficult  and this is certainly one of them but  she's going to have a number of  continued engagements this week and we  are certainly hopeful we can get it  across the finish line  jen there was lots to talk to you about  you guys made a lot of news this week  thank you thanks for joining us  you too

